WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
By the end of Act 4, a magician has
every man who wronged him in his power:

2
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.950
"Lies at my mercy all mine enemies."

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.790
In a revenge tragedy, this
is where vengeance falls.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.080
But in Act 5, his spirit servant
speaks up for the prisoners:

5
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.710
"Mine would, sir, were I human."

6
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.370
And he forgives them.

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.980
So why would a man with total power
let the men who wronged him go?

8
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.630
In this mission, you'll see how
the play sets up a revenge plot,

9
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.270
and then turns it.

10
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.570
You'll read Prospero's
reply to the spirit,

11
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.020
line by line.

12
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.970
And you'll ask who is truly
forgiven, and who is truly set free.

13
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: explain why
Prospero forgives his enemies.
